<title>USA: Chesapeake start-up costs hurt Q3.</title>
<headline>Chesapeake start-up costs hurt Q3.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chesapeake Corp, reporting lower third quarter results on Monday, cited weaker market conditions in the kraft paper business and start-up costs from growth initiatives in the packaging and tissue units.</p>
<p>It said its growth intiatives include the acquisition of a point-of-sale display business, a two-year plan to double manufacturing capability for its consumer graphics packaging busness, and the acquisition of Chesapeake Europe SA.</p>
</text>
